<task id="to_attach_a_file_in_salesforce_to_a_new_emails_0fd44f" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To attach a file in Salesforce to a new emails</title>
   <shortdesc>Prerequisites</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">user-0266f</author>
      <critdates>
         <revised modified="Nov 05, 2018"/>
      </critdates>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>attach</keyword>
        <keyword>click</keyword>
        <keyword>Salesforce</keyword>
        <keyword>emails</keyword>
        <keyword>Outlook</keyword>
        <keyword>select</keyword>
        <indexterm>attach</indexterm>
        <indexterm>click</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Salesforce</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>
            <b>Prerequisites</b>
         </p>
         <p>The X-Author Outlook add-in must have been installed and you are connected.</p>
         <p>
            <b>Steps</b>
         </p>
      </context>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>In Outlook, click <b>New E-mail</b> and from the <b>Message</b> tab select Attach Salesforce File.

The default is to use Chatter files. To change this to Attachments, click <b>Show Criteria</b> and select <b>Attachments.</b>
            </cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98671240</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98671234/98671240.jpg" width="288" height="97" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Enter a name or partial name for the object record which contains the file you want to attach and click.</cmd>
            <info>
               <image href="../attachments/98671234/98671239.jpg" width="21" height="16" placement="inline">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Select</b> beside the object that contains the file and then click <b>Open</b> besides the file you want to attach.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <p>
            <b>Results</b>
         </p>
         <p>The file is now attached to the draft email.</p>
         <p>
            <b>What's Next</b>
         </p>
         <p>You can repeat the task to attach another file or send the email.</p>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>